  "review": "Root inspected raw Linux USB enumeration and usbmuxd logs. Original service API QueryType identified com.apple.mobile.restored version15. Clean first iOS shutdown removed device; same Linux VM enumerated the second iOS process as USB device003. Root independently ran lsusb, idevice_id and the read-only restored query over loopback SSH; all succeeded. The query source is retained. No restore transaction was started. This proves recovery USB/control service, not installed iOS, app launch, touch, or performance. The Linux serial artifact is a snapshot taken after root reconnect verification; complete logs remain at full_report paths.",
  "later_duration_outcome": "Reconnected recovery subsequently reached its 120-second idle wait-for-restore timeout and panicked during shutdown (Halt/Restart Timed Out). Emulator exit0 at about160s does not establish completion of the requested300s duration. USB/service/reconnect success was verified before that separate failure. Linux companion subsequently powered down cleanly."
